{
  "title": "Winnipeg Nights — translating speech on one core",
  "alt": "Audio is cut into short fixed windows and each window is handed to a local speech model asked to translate directly rather than transcribe and then translate. The smallest model is used deliberately, because the host has a single core and a model that cannot keep up with real time produces a translation that falls further behind every minute.",
